 ground, so POL-RD-13(1) applies and this is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. The case is therefore decided on the record, and there is no POL-RD-06 repeat-pattern finding (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 250 completed trips).\n\nResult: NO_ACTION. The SGD 10.29 charged stands exactly as it is; nothing is refunded and nothing is paid to the driver. The rider's grievance — being set down short of her pin and having to run the last stretch with two small children — is real and is recorded on the trip record itself, but the route-deviation policy prices excess distance, not a short stop, and on this record there is no excess to price. If the rider wishes to pursue the short dropoff as a service-quality concern, that is a separate matter from this fare."
  },
