    "explanation": "This is a route-deviation dispute on trip TRP-00536, and it fails at the first gate. POL-RD-01 measures a deviation as the excess of the trace distance over the booked optimal. The governing figure is gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 3.09 km (EV-GPS-00536), set against the booked optimal_distance_km of 3.2 km (EV-TRIP-00536). The excess is -0.11 km, or -3.44%: the driven distance is shorter than the booked optimal. Neither establishment test is passed — the excess is not greater than 20% of optimal and not greater than 0.8 km — and POL-RD-01 is explicit that where either test fails no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. Both advocates' threshold claims are accepted: the rider's concession that she presses no POL-RD-02 recomputation and the driver's reading of the governing trace figure agree, and the trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (73 fixes, 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, maximum inter-fix gap 0.0 s, no gap over 90 s and no jump over 500 m), so no POL-RD-07 impairment and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises.\n\nThe driver's 'the last stretch is a bus lane' explanation (counterparty statement) and the rider's citation of the traffic advisory are answered together. The advisory EV-ADVIS-00536-01 is MISSING from the bundle at weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the driver's traffic-cause assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Under POL-RD-13 it is also not a POL-RD-10(5) trigger, because the driver named no advisory evidence ID: the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact. Nothing turns on it here in any event, because there is no deviation to excuse.\n\nThe rider's real grievance is recorded and I accept it. The trip_record dropoff label reads 'Marina Coastal Dr, 210 m short of the pier', and the driver's own statement concedes stopping about 200 metres short of the pin. But the policy prices a route deviation, not an incomplete trip. POL-RD-05 (dropoff relocation) cannot run: pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so there is no amended endpoint and no re-quote to re-test. POL-RD-01 measures only the distance between the recorded pickup and dropoff events and registers nothing about a trip ending short of its pinned destination. No clause in POLICY-ROUTE-DEVIATION produces a refund for a short-ended drop, and POL-RD-09(4) reaches only unmatched gantry lines and wrongly applied surcharges. The fare ledger reconciles line by line — base 3.80 + distance 2.33 + time 3.36 + platform fee 0.80 = 10.29 charged (EV-FARE-00536), with no ERP gantry, no toll and no airport surcharge — so no billing-integrity correction is due.\n\nThe chat log (EV-CHAT-00536) contains zero messages, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable to either side, and the driver's profile shows no repeat deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 250 completed_trips_90d), so POL-RD-06 gives no full-refund uplift and licenses no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral. No clause on this record produces a referral.\n\nThe outcome is NO_ACTION: the filing party's claim is not supported by the evidence and the present state stands. On this rider-filed dispute, with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, the SGD 10.29 charge is left in place and nothing is returned. Confidence is 0.9, capped by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts (EV-GPS-00536 and EV-TRIP-00536). One matter is left open for support rather than for a referral: the short-ended drop, and the platform messages the rider says told her she 'couldn't reach me', concern service completion and are outside this route-deviation policy; the rider may raise them through in-app support."
